  "review_notes": [
    "The backend candidate image retains high and medium Debian OS-package findings. They remain open; no critical findings were reported by this image scan.",
    "The frontend candidate image had no vulnerabilities reported by Trivy 0.74.0 for this ARM64 build.",
    "KSV-0125 findings remain open because the manifests use release-placeholder image references and no registry allowlist approval exists.",
    "AWS-0132 remains unsuppressed: S3 access-log destination encryption uses SSE-S3 per AWS server-access logging guidance, while Trivy requests a customer-managed KMS key. This tooling conflict requires review and is not treated as an approved exception.",
    "AWS-0089 remains open for the access-log destination bucket; no scanner ignore was added.",
    "The backend and frontend Dockerfiles run apt/apk package upgrades from signed live distribution repositories. This hardens the built images but means future rebuilds can change image digests; every build must be rescanned and recorded.",
    "Candidate images are ARM64 only, local, and unsigned. SBOMs are inventory reports, not release provenance."
  ],
